WHAT THE PATCHES DO

crdroid_oplus_ltpo_readback.patch
  The LTPO settings screen reads the panel's current adfr_config mask when it is
  opened and on resume, instead of showing the last stored preference. A missing
  or malformed response disables the toggle rather than presenting a stored wish
  as the current state. Writing, flushing, closing and an exact read-back of the
  mask must all succeed before a selection is stored; on failure the screen shows
  the actual configuration value where it can be read.

crdroid_oplus_touch_error_handling.patch
  GloveMode checks the Binder status, negative driver write responses and the read
  format; empty or malformed answers are reported as an error. The existing
  "status:counter" format stays valid and only the first field determines the
  reported on/off state. TouchscreenGesture accepts only configured keycodes,
  bounded before subtraction and shifting, and parses the full hexadecimal mask
  response without throwing. The resulting decimal mask must fit into eight bytes
  before any write, because longer values are ignored by the driver while it still
  reports success. Both touch write steps check the Binder status and a negative
  driver result; after the first failure no second write is attempted. The power
  double-tap path additionally validates the vendor proxy.

  No gesture node, gesture list or touch sampling rate is modified.
